  "task": "Find out why Retrieve calls (bedrock-agent-runtime Retrieve / RetrieveAndGenerate) against the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Base named 'llmops-lf-kb-vsgone' have started failing, even though the KB status is ACTIVE and its latest ingestion job shows COMPLETE.",
  "context": "User wants the root cause explained in chat. Read-only work only: do NOT make any mutating AWS calls. Account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1. First resolve the KB id via bedrock-agent list_knowledge_bases, then get_knowledge_base, list_data_sources, list_ingestion_jobs. Determine the exact error the callers see (error code/message), when failures began, and what changed just before.",
  "resources": ["Bedrock knowledge base: llmops-lf-kb-vsgone", "account 012345678901_1", "us-east-1", "KB service role, vector store (e.g. OpenSearch Serverless collection / Aurora / other configured store), embedding model, any KMS keys, Bedrock model invocation logging log groups, CloudWatch logs for calling apps/Lambdas"],
  "timeframe": "Last 7 days up to 2026-11-25T10:15:00Z; find the first failure time and compare to the baseline before it",
  "criteria": "Check: (1) KB config and vector store config/health (does the backing index/collection/cluster/DB still exist and is it reachable; index name, field mappings, dimension match with embedding model); (2) the KB service role permissions and trust policy, and data access policies / network policies for OpenSearch Serverless or Secrets Manager/RDS permissions for the store; (3) embedding model access/availability (model access, model ID, region, throttling or quota); (4) KMS key policy/state if encryption is used; (5) caller-side permissions (IAM for bedrock:Retrieve on the KB ARN, SCPs, resource policies, VPC endpoint policies); (6) CloudTrail changes (use lookup_cloudtrail_events) to the KB, data source, vector store, IAM roles/policies, KMS, collection policies, model access around the first failure; (7) CloudWatch logs/metrics/Bedrock invocation logs for the actual error messages and throttling/quota signals; (8) whether sync COMPLETE hides issues such as zero indexed docs or failed document counts (look at ingestion job statistics: numberOfDocumentsFailed, numberOfDocumentsDeleted, etc.) . Report the most likely root cause with the supporting evidence (exact error text, timestamps, the specific change/event), what you ruled out, and a suggested fix. Be explicit about what is confirmed vs hypothesis."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Investigate Bedrock KB Retrieve failures in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

